@meta
id: 13-14
title: Drill — very magic by reflex
chapter: 13
type: drill
skills: regex-verymagic, regex-quantifiers
par: 30
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: read every line, find the one without a caret or a tilde
open: package.json

@brief
Eight times: one dependency in this file is pinned to an exact version
with no `^` in front of it. Find it and give it the caret.

The shape is a quote, three numbers with dots between them, a quote.
Type it in very magic, every time, without stopping to think about
which characters need a backslash.

@keys
| `\v` | very magic |
| `\d+` | one or more digits, no backslash on the plus |
| `\.` | a literal dot — still escaped, even under `\v` |
| `a` | append after the cursor |

@hints
The caret-less version is the one where the digit sits directly after
the opening quote. Put the quote in the pattern.
--
`/\v"\d+\.\d+\.\d+"` `Enter` lands on the opening quote. `a^` and
`Esc`.

@solution
/\v"\d+\.\d+\.\d+"<Enter>  a^<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Twenty-six keystrokes, and the pattern is one you have typed in
`grep`, in a test, in a validation rule. Under `\v` it is the same
pattern here.

By rep four the `\v` should be the first thing your fingers do after
`/`, before you have decided what the pattern is. By rep eight the
`\.` should be automatic too — the dot is the one character that is
special in *every* dialect, so it needs its escape everywhere.

@start package.json
{
  "name": "order-service",
  "version": "0.3.0-beta.4",
  "private": true,
  "dependencies": {
